=base:main-content.cmark

# About

Salmon is written by Lucas DiCioccio, who also writes about it, and about
the other tools it grows alongside, on his blog at
[dicioccio.fr](https://dicioccio.fr/). The source is on
[GitHub](https://github.com/lucasdicioccio/salmon).

This site is itself generated by a salmon binary, `salmon-docs-sync`, which
rebuilds the pages with Kitchen Sink from the repository's `resources/` and
`specs/` directories.

## Sibling sites

- [Kitchen Sink](https://kitchensink-tech.github.io/) — the static-site
  generator this site is made with, and whose `documentation` layout the
  guides and specs use.
- [tramaj](https://lucasdicioccio.github.io/tramaj/) — the templating
  language of Kitchen Sink's sections.
- [agents-exe](https://lucasdicioccio.github.io/agents-exe/) — a runner for
  LLM agents.
- [acme-not-a-joke](https://lucasdicioccio.github.io/acme-not-a-joke/) — the
  ACME client behind salmon's certificate-signing recipes
  (`salmon-ops-recipes-experimental`).

